#basePath	Day2

:: BeginDay
@trigger    SceneReady
@boostScore 100
@who    Astrid

$call MoveToView("Left")
{@Astrid} Looks like I got some mail.
$call StopPuzzleMode()
$call StopOpenMode()
$call SpawnDocumentToCamera("Day2DadPostcard")
{@Astrid} A postcard from Dad.
$call SetInputState(true)

:: SpawnPuzzleDocs1
@trigger    DocumentInspectEnd
@when   documentId == "Day2DadPostcard"
@once

$call Wait(1)
$call SpawnDocumentToCamera("Day2ElijahPostcard")
{@Astrid} And one from Elijah.

:: SpawnPuzzleDocs2
@trigger    DocumentInspectEnd
@when   documentId == "Day2ElijahPostcard"
@once

{@Astrid} Where is Elijah? Is he okay?
$call StartDocumentPuzzle("Day2DocumentPuzzle")

:: IncorrectDocumentResponse
@trigger    DocumentPuzzlePromptStart
@when documentId != "Day2ElijahPostcard"

{@Astrid} I don't think that's right...

:: CorrectDocumentResponse
@trigger    DocumentPuzzlePromptStart
@when documentId == "Day2ElijahPostcard"
@once

{@Astrid} This is it!
$call Wait(2)

$call SetInputState(false)
$call MoveToView("Right")
{@Radio} Star HQ to Station Seven.
IceCube is reading a high-energy neutrino emission from the area of the Hydra Constellation. 
Identification of nearby celestial objects is requested. 
Uploading area of interest... (*beeeep screeech boop beep boop beeeep*)

$call WaitForMovedToView("Desk")
$call StartNeutrinoNavigation()
$call SetInputState(true)

:: NeutrinoNavigationComplete
@trigger    NeutrinoNavigationComplete
@once

{@Radio} Neutrino Origin Detected
$call StopNeutrinoNavigation()
$call StartOpenMode()

:: PointsUpdated
@trigger    PointsUpdated
@when   sciencePoints > 2
@once

$call StopOpenMode()
$call ClearMonitorSelection()
$call SetInputState(false)
{@Dad} Astrid, this is Dad. Nice work on the first puzzle!
I’ve got more information for you on Project Hercules. 
Long story short—there’s a satellite out there in space with a ton of data about the night sky!

{@Astrid} What?! How is that even possible? I thought everything was destroyed!
$call Wait(1)

{@Dad} The satellite was put in orbit by the guy who funded Elijah’s old lab.
Sort of a secret back-up plan, in case anything ever happened.
Astrid, if we could unlock this satellite, it would change everything.
We could access data that we thought was lost forever. And we’d be able to use the satellite to communicate!
It sure would be good to hear your voice again.
$call Wait(1)
 
{@Astrid} Wow. Dad, that’s amazing!
$call Wait(1)
 
{@Dad} Now I know you’re probably wondering what’s the deal with the puzzles.
Sounds like this guy was sort of . . . well, a kind way to put it might be “eccentric.”
He encrypted the satellite, so that only other astronomers could access it. 
Each puzzle reveals part of the password.
$call Wait(1)
 
{@Astrid} Okay . . . so these puzzles reveal the password to the satellite. Got it.
Elijah said he was updating each station. He must be getting them ready to connect to Project Hercules!
$call Wait(1)

{@Dad} Okay, Little Bear, I gotta go for now. This frequency is regulated. 
$call Wait(1)

{@Astrid} Dad, wait! I think there’s something else going on with Elijah.
$call Wait(1)

{@Dad} Your next puzzle is the constellation Hercules.
See if Elijah’s notes can point you in the right direction.
I’ll check in as soon as I can. Love you, Little Bear. 
$call Wait(1)

{@Astrid}Dad?
$call Wait(1)
Ugh. I still don’t get it.
$call Wait(1)
Elijah said we might be too late. Too late for what?
Why does he always have to be so cryptic?

$call SetInputState(true)
$call StartPuzzleNavigation()

:: PuzzleNavigationComplete
@trigger    PuzzleNavigationComplete
@once

$call StopPuzzleNavigation()
{@Radio} This is where an instrument unlock would happen.
{@Radio} Unlocking now. Stand By...
$call StartPuzzleMode()

:: HerculesPuzzleComplete
@trigger    CorrectPuzzleSubmission
@when   puzzleName == "Hercules"
@once

$call ClearMonitorSelection()
$call StopPuzzleMode()
$call SetInputState(false)
{@Astrid} Time to turn in for the night.
Oh, what's this?
$call EndDay2->BeginCutscene()

:: EndDay
@trigger    CutsceneEnd
@when cutsceneId == "EndDay2"
@who    Radio

$call LoadNextDay()